  "physical_reading": "The whole Hesse non-Clifford outcome alphabet can be displayed as one 72-tick microframe: each of the nine eraser-lift outcomes owns one 8-tick return word that erases the branch, records route and phase, applies X/Z frame correction, stores the T-frame bit, and restores the Clifford packet ABI.",
  "html_scope": "docs/bt1404_holonet_scope.html",
  "boundary": "BT1404 is a packet-scope/ABI visualization and verifier. It does not implement physical SIC optics, detector electronics, or a magic-state factory."
